                ],
                "steps": [
                    {
                        "recipe_order": 7,
                        "step": "Anaerobically dispense liquid minimal medium in 10-ml portions into 100-ml serum vials under an atmosphere of N2/CO2 (80:20). Seal vials with butyl rubber stoppers secured with aluminium crimp seals. Sterilize by autoclaving for 15 minutes at 121\u00b0C. Prior to inoculation, pressurize bottles to 2 x 102 kPa with H2/CO2. For solidified plating medium, add the following components per liter of liquid minimal medium: "
                    },
                    {
                        "step": "Add titanium(III) citrate solution to warm (60\u00b0C) agar medium after autoclaving. For preparation of solidified agar medium."
                    }
                ],
